{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-3","kind":"proposition","title":"求两个可公度量的最大公度","englishTitle":"Given two commensurable magnitudes, to find their greatest common measure.","book":10,"number":3,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.3","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.3/","group":"prop_1","sourceNumber":3,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","contentId":"euclid-10-3","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"cd9433579151e269688051a1b1bad18355ed873c30ad59fb3f8b797fdd0e51db","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-3.statement","euclid-10-3.construction.1","euclid-10-3.proof.1","euclid-10-3.proof.2","euclid-10-3.proof.3","euclid-10-3.proof.4","euclid-10-3.proof.5","euclid-10-3.proof.6","euclid-10-3.proof.7","euclid-10-3.proof.8","euclid-10-3.proof.9","euclid-10-3.proof.10","euclid-10-3.proof.11","euclid-10-3.proof.12","euclid-10-3.construction.2","euclid-10-3.proof.13","euclid-10-3.proof.14","euclid-10-3.proof.15","euclid-10-3.proof.16","euclid-10-3.proof.17","euclid-10-3.proof.18","euclid-10-3.proof.19","euclid-10-3.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-3.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"fcaa09bbea23d8e62f774db67c8fb2106fdc3119eac8790ca13dd2fe06027f54","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Given two commensurable magnitudes, to find their greatest common measure."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"以两张可公度的尺码 来找到它们最大的共同标准；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"67a7e0310d8dee1939edfa79276489095b532225223b7dd7b396c6038cb73fd6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let the two given commensurable magnitudes be AB, CD of which AB is the less; thus it is required to find the greatest common measure of AB, CD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"给定的可公度级为AB,CD,其中AB为较小数量;因此,需要找到最大共同度量为AB,CD；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"44e9fdcacea914e409a4c1d0b92d60ac2e2b2943f460e1feceb65ebeb5921566","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now the magnitude AB either measures CD or it does not."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在AB级的量度要么是CD,要么不是"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0a32b198b6c282b1b522d97bb421a4b3ce35a6e21ed66670506a636dccb0f250","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If then it measures it—and it measures itself also—AB is a common measure of AB, CD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果当时它衡量它——而且它也衡量它本身——AB是AB,CD的共同衡量标准。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"999d56b8cab60ba3b4489f7336adfd5858f46528e7f922158045f7edc5afcedf","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And it is manifest that it is also the greatest; for a greater magnitude than the magnitude AB will not measure AB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"很明显,它也是最大的;如果比AB级的大小更大,则无法测量AB级。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"cdc55871f8b347a96b76048eeb06b48392cf48f1054e5d0f134f0564a703b018","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Next, let AB not measure CD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"接下来,让AB不测量CD。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e1aa84a971189d49895e3116003d0f1deac9992e33cbc14e28f800034efbb97a","citations":["euclid-10-2"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Then, if the less be continually subtracted in turn from the greater, that which is left over will sometime measure the one before it, because AB, CD are not incommensurable; [cf. [X. 2](/principles/euclid-10-2)] let AB, measuring ED, leave EC less than itself, let EC, measuring FB, leave AF less than itself, and let AF measure CE."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果从较大数量中不断减去较小数量,则剩下的数量将有时测量到它面前的数量,因为AB,CD不是不可公度;] AB, ED, EC, FB, FB, AF, CE, AF, CE。 [cf. [X. 2](/principles/euclid-10-2)"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1b40d077f9de0555e6cd20e5139ffe645818d8142b4506a389e900e5fa8fe542","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since, then, AF measures CE, while CE measures FB, therefore AF will also measure FB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"此后,AF项措施CE项,CE项措施FB项,因此AF项措施也将FB项。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ce41a10df4b7dcd06302eda7c4728302c7657716c49c6bb318937643058c74aa","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures itself also; therefore AF will also measure the whole AB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,它本身也衡量;因此,AF项也将衡量整个AB项。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1ccceea6a9a6439e7c75463edcd16ab5c6ba518c1f39241daa8c29793a0f1113","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But AB measures DE; therefore AF will also measure ED."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但AB项措施DE,因此AF项措施也将ED。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.9","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":10,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 9","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6d6e8618d566ee23c65b7d3e3d3531d1253e2657c2fb71367f202f887a5f2ccd","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures CE also; therefore it also measures the whole CD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但它也衡量CE;因此它也衡量整个CD。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.10","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":11,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 10","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"71e11fa262ce78f829886a951ca02e6de2370e01155337478538161cb5b40789","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore AF is a common measure of AB, CD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,AF是AB,CD的共同计量标准。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.11","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":12,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 11","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8d601a2226cb30a3cfb5f77868366f58ff9f45ffd66f31803b59b1f868041374","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"I say next that it is also the greatest."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"我接下来说,这也是最伟大的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.12","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":13,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 12","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"57615c1a022d9fed682fe48b901ae55e75da7349ab4eee3d4173b5e40046e066","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if not, there will be some magnitude greater than AF which will measure AB, CD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"否则,将出现超过AF的数值,将测量AB,CD。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":14,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f4120114a8bddfc745eaad1a5cb1fd24fece05ee7f44fd92cf2064099f2ed8c2","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let it be G."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"G块吧"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.13","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":15,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 13","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e2bc28a92532036e6ef0597f9ce9823702882fdd53ddd844eace5629f72247c7","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then G measures AB, while AB measures ED, therefore G will also measure ED."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"自那时以来,G项措施AB项,AB项措施ED项,因此,G项措施也将ED项。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.14","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":16,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 14","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"4b947d918ee69ea0c58b3fc6c4f07bd46416435f21fa9d1a0b28f57275e5efdc","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures the whole CD also; therefore G will also measure the remainder CE."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是它也衡量了整个CD;因此,G也将衡量其余的CE。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.15","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":17,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 15","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f3dd526331b7b886c44032c459a7294768834c1068db456c184cd0ba3df94a06","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But CE measures FB; therefore G will also measure FB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但CE项措施FB,因此G项措施也将FB。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.16","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":18,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 16","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9e9fd0ab30306fead8fddff09ae86677540b42eccd8754065512457924bafcfa","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures the whole AB also, and it will therefore measure the remainder AF, the greater the less: which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但它也测量了整个AB,因此它测量了其余的AF,数量越大,数量就越小:这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.17","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":19,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 17","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0449ecf457f1bd51d15f40e0510b0e07a9afbb1c94f3b68d52097a726842182d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore no magnitude greater than AF will measure AB, CD; therefore AF is the greatest common measure of AB, CD."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,不超过AF的数值将测量AB,CD;因此,AF是AB,CD这一最大共同数值；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.18","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":20,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 18","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"4415ea6426e07957467c3bf4525bf802fb2c0b8b627f996a26da83fe5b77077d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the greatest common measure of the two given commensurable magnitudes AB, CD has been found. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,发现给定的可公度级AB、CD的最大共同度量为Q. E.D；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.proof.19","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":21,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 19","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c5b5712df6b3b0c197644a2a4b66da1b532c5ac96dcb687a89145b18c56c23fd","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Porism. From this it is manifest that, if a magnitude measure two magnitudes, it will also measure their greatest common measure."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"普罗里斯姆,从这一点来看,很明显,如果一个量测量两个量,它也将测量它们最大的共同量；其中所求的量是最大公约数。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-3.source","contentId":"euclid-10-3","revisionId":"euclid-10-3@raw-cd9433579151e269","order":22,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"30b702aa6883ffc537e72baabec694a99969f693c9025c4af5536c6b12e80a6c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.3/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.3\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-3:euclid-10-2:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-3.proof.5"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-2","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.3","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.3/","sourceLabel":"X. 2"}}],"incomingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-4:euclid-10-3:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-4","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-4.construction.2","euclid-10-4.proof.6","euclid-10-4.proof.8","euclid-10-4.proof.13","euclid-10-4.proof.15"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-3","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.4","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.4/","sourceLabel":"X. 3"}}],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-10-3:euclid-10-2:explicit","id":"euclid-10-2","book":10,"number":2,"kind":"proposition","title":"辗转相减不停机与不可公度","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-10-4:euclid-10-3:explicit","id":"euclid-10-4","book":10,"number":4,"kind":"proposition","title":"求三个可公度量的最大公度","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"visualization":{"level":"concept_illustration","rendererId":"concept-irrational","rationale":"The current renderer is selected by a broad geometry family and must not be presented as this proposition’s exact construction."},"sourceIssues":[]}
